    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Zinc; it reacts vigorously with dilute non-oxidising acids to liberate \(\text{H}_2\) gas.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Titanium; it becomes passive in concentrated oxidising acids due to protective oxide formation.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Manganese; it exhibits an exceptionally high oxidation state of \(+7\) in aqueous solution.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Copper; it is unable to liberate \(\text{H}_2\) gas from dilute mineral acids because its high atomisation and ionisation energies are not compensated by hydration energy.</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
