<p>In the diagram, the ionic radii of \(\text{M}^{3+}\) ions decrease smoothly across the series, whereas points for \(\text{Eu}^{2+}\) and \(\text{Yb}^{2+}\) lie distinctly above the trivalent curve, and \(\text{Ce}^{4+}\) and \(\text{Tb}^{4+}\) lie below it. What electronic configurations account for the extra stability of \(\text{Eu}^{2+}\) and \(\text{Tb}^{4+}\), respectively?</p>
